  "details": "This is an issue that only started happening with the big controls overhaul update.\n\nEven if I turn off haptic feedback in the settings, I get haptic feedback every time I press my Triggers on my Vive Wands (1.0) - even if I'm not grabbing or interacting with anything. I could be pressing trigger in the air with nothing around, typing, or pressing trigger to use my Fist gesture, and my controller will rumble. The behavior wasn't like this before and it has been wearing down my battery like crazy and is extremely annoying. The haptic feedback stops when I'm in OVR or SteamVR Desktop, so it's 100% VRChat.",
